# Everything here is regenerated by `bash run_bm651_e2e.sh` from tracked sources
# (rung5/*.asm + *.py, bm651_construct.py, bm651_img2.asm), so the row's evidence
# is evidence/, not these. *.bin / *.raw / *.log are already ignored upstream.
/defs_*.txt
/bm651_*.png
/bm651_*.json
/bm651_*.raw
/bm651_fixtures.txt
/stage1_const.inc
/rung5_layout.inc
/*.lst

# BM653 (option C): every one of these is a build product of
# `bash run_bm653_e2e.sh`, which regenerates the forked loader, the per-variant
# geometry includes, the seven media and the captures from tracked sources
# (rung6/*.asm + rung9/*.py imported, bm653_construct/img2/pxcodec/mkimg). The
# row's evidence is evidence/bm653/ -- transcripts, dumps, the prediction file
# as derived, and the loader text that actually ran -- not these.
/build/
/fixtures/
/captures/
/scope653/
/bm653_stage2_px*.asm
/bm653_px_*.inc
/bm653_img2_scribbler.asm
/bm653_capture.py
/bm653_px_meta.json
/bm653_fixtures.json

# The one deliberate exception upstream's `*.bin` would swallow:
# evidence/refs/ holds the PINNED copies of BM903's leg-0 handoff dumps that
# bm653_identity.py compares against, so they are reference bytes, not build
# products — rung9 rewrites its own working copies at every capture leg, which
# is why this row keeps its own (see RECEIPT_BM653.md, defect #11, and
# `python3 bm653_refs.py --check`). Negated rather than force-added so the
# exception survives the next `git add`.
!/evidence/refs/*.bin
